@startuml
title One beta step, end to end: `(lam x. x, lam a. lam b. a)` reduces to `lam a. lam b. a`

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam ParticipantPadding 12
skinparam BoxPadding 12
skinparam participant {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}

participant "**source text**\n`(lam x. x, lam a. lam b. a)`" as SRC #DCFCE7
participant "**parser.rs**\nPratt / WPDA" as PARSE #DBEAFE
participant "**set automaton**\npositional matcher" as MATCH #EDE9FE
participant "**Beta rule**\n`(App (Lam fun) arg)`\n`~> (eval fun arg)`" as BETA #FCE7F3
participant "**subst.rs**\ncapture-avoiding\nsubstitution engine" as SUBST #FEF3C7
participant "**normal form**" as NF #DCFCE7

SRC -> PARSE : token stream\n`(` `lam ` `x` `.` `x` `,` `lam ` ... `)`
PARSE -> MATCH : ""App(Lam(Scope(x, TVar x)),""\n""    Lam(Scope(a, Lam(Scope(b, TVar a)))))""

group Match the redex (symbol-once descent)
  MATCH -> MATCH : head is `App`, arity 2
  MATCH -> MATCH : descend child 0 -> head is `Lam`, arity 1
  MATCH -> MATCH : capture child 0's **Scope** as `fun`\n(binder AND body, not the opened body)
  MATCH -> MATCH : capture child 1 as `arg`
end

MATCH -> BETA : sigma = { fun |-> Scope(x, TVar x),\n            arg |-> Lam(Scope(a, Lam(Scope(b, TVar a)))) }

BETA -> SUBST : RHS `(eval fun arg)` is the two-argument form\n-> `MultiSubst { scope: fun, replacements: [arg] }`

group Contract: <latex>(\lambda x.\,M)\,N \;\rightsquigarrow\; M[N/x]</latex>
  SUBST -> SUBST : `unbind` the scope (FRESHENS the binder)
  SUBST -> SUBST : walk the body, replacing bound occurrences of `x` by `arg`
  SUBST -> SUBST : body is exactly the bound occurrence -> result is `arg`
end

SUBST -> NF : ""Lam(Scope(a, Lam(Scope(b, TVar a))))""
NF -> NF : no `App` node remains -> no rule matches -> **normal form**

note over NF
  Printed by display.rs as `lam a . lam b . a` — the K combinator.
end note

note over MATCH, BETA
  `Beta` has an EMPTY premise list (`Beta . |- ...`), so it fires on
  SHAPE ALONE. The three congruence rules carry a `S ~> T` premise
  and are what license firing at a NON-ROOT position.
end note

@enduml
